12. PARTIAL EXIT PREVIEW BUG WE FIXED
============================================================

Initial preview logic treated Partial Exit as if the entered quantity were
the entry quantity.

Original calculation was effectively:

const previewEntryValue =
  previewQuantity *
  previewEntryPrice *
  previewMultiplier;

const previewExitValue =
  previewQuantity *
  previewExitPrice *
  previewMultiplier;

const previewGrossPnL =
  tradeType === "COMPLETE"
    ? ...
    : 0;

That was incorrect for Partial Exit.

Example:

Existing position:

20 shares @ $100

Partial Exit:

8 shares @ $110

The preview must NOT calculate entry value as:

8 × $100 = $800

because the historical position was originally entered as:

20 × $100 = $2,000

The realized P&L, however, must be calculated only for the quantity being
closed:

8 shares.

Therefore we changed the preview calculations to use the selected
existing position's entry price and quantity for Entry Value, while using
the Partial Exit quantity for realized P&L.

The current working block is:

const previewEntryPriceForExit =
  Number(selectedPreviewPosition?.entryPrice ?? 0);

const previewEntryQuantityForExit =
  Number(selectedPreviewPosition?.quantity ?? 0);

const previewEntryValue =
  isPartialExit
    ? previewEntryPriceForExit *
      previewEntryQuantityForExit *
      previewMultiplier
    : previewQuantity *
      previewEntryPrice *
      previewMultiplier;

const previewExitValue =
  previewQuantity *
  previewExitPrice *
  previewMultiplier;

const previewGrossPnL =
  tradeType === "COMPLETE"
    ? side === "LONG"
      ? previewExitValue - previewEntryValue
      : previewEntryValue - previewExitValue
    : isPartialExit
      ? side === "LONG"
        ? (previewExitPrice -
            previewEntryPriceForExit) *
          previewQuantity *
          previewMultiplier
        : (previewEntryPriceForExit -
            previewExitPrice) *
          previewQuantity *
          previewMultiplier
      : 0;

