24. FIFO / pairTrades
============================================================

The FIFO engine remains protected.

It reconstructs trades from executions.

It supports:

- Opening execution
- Closing execution
- Open remainder
- Multiple partial exits
- Deterministic FIFO consumption

Example:

BUY 100

SELL 25
SELL 25
SELL 50

results in lifecycle realization through separate consumption
events with final closed state.

No FIFO rewrite was performed.

============================================================
25. IMPORTANT DESIGN PRINCIPLE
============================================================

Manual lifecycle operations must manipulate executions, not
directly manipulate derived trades.

Therefore:

EDIT PARTIAL EXIT
→ replace exact exit execution
→ pairTrades reconstructs trades

DELETE PARTIAL EXIT
→ delete exact exit execution
→ pairTrades reconstructs trades

PARTIAL ENTRY
→ add opening execution
→ pairTrades reconstructs lifecycle

OPEN POSITION
→ one opening execution
→ pairTrades emits OPEN trade

COMPLETE
→ entry + exit executions
→ pairTrades reconstructs closed trade

This architecture remains canonical.

